<title>USA: Chevron to reveal Kazakstan oil profit - NYT.</title>
<headline>Chevron to reveal Kazakstan oil profit - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chevron Corp is expected to tell stock analysts today that it made more than $80 million last year from its Kazakstan oilfield, the New York Times said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Chevron's 1995 profits from the venture were only $1.0 million, the paper said, adding that that analysts differed over whether the pipeline earnings would significantly affect the company's share price.</p>
<p>The announcement was expected from Jeet Bindra, president of the Chevron Pipe Line Company, at a meeting in New York City today, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
